139b0efc8b3183006b6617dc1afe12ff1e9de6ae441b04935504909c1c","file":"preprints/The-Stable-Hurewicz-Image-of-the-Sphere-at-Two-September-25-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":24,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"24e1c95c2c136493d990b5972b35e14b2da6acdb0987d2fd28b7f5a54930d842","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Stable-Hurewicz-Image-of-the-Sphere-at-Two-September-25-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5a7e9d139b0efc8b3183006b6617dc1afe12ff1e9de6ae441b04935504909c1c","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Stable-Hurewicz-Image-of-the-Sphere-at-Two-September-25-2026/build/introduction.tex#L24"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:curtis}\nThe image of \\(\\bigoplus_{d>0}h_d\\) is spanned over \\(\\F_2\\) by\nthe Hurewicz images of the Hopf-invariant-one classes\n\\(\\eta,\\nu,\\sigma\\), in degrees \\(1,3,7\\), and the\nKervaire-invariant-one classes \\(\\theta_j\\), in degrees\n\\(2^{j+1}-2\\), \\(j\\ge1\\), whenever they exist.\nIn particular, Curtis's conjecture is true in all positive degrees."}
